<section class="slide w">
<h2>Past Simple (I did)</h2>
<div class="q">Mozart <b>was</b> an Austrian musician and composer. He <b>lived</b> from 1756 to 1791. He <b>started</b> composing at the age of five and <b>wrote</b> more than 600 pieces of music. He <b>was</b> only 35 years old when he <b>died</b>.</div>
<div class="g">
<div class="q"><b class="l">Regular verbs end in -ed</b>invite → <span class="a rv">invited</span> &nbsp; stop → <span class="a rv">stopped</span> &nbsp; study → <span class="a rv">studied</span><br>Laura <b>passed</b> her exam because she <b>studied</b> very hard.<br>They <b>invited</b> us to their party, but we <b>decided</b> not to go.</div>
<div class="q"><b class="l">Irregular verbs do not end in -ed</b>write → <b>wrote</b> &nbsp; see → <b>saw</b>go → <b>went</b> &nbsp; shut → <b>shut</b><br>I <b>went</b> to the cinema three times last week.</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="slide b">
<h2>Past Simple: Questions and Negatives</h2>
<div class="g">
<div class="q"><b class="l">did + infinitive (question)</b>Did you <b>enjoy</b> it?<br>How many people did they <b>invite</b> to the wedding?</div>
<div class="q"><b class="l">didn't + infinitive (negative)</b>I didn't <b>buy</b> anything because I didn't <b>have</b> any money.</div>
</div>
<div class="q"><b class="l">The past of be (am/is/are) is was/were</b>I/he/she/it <b>was/wasn't</b> &nbsp;|&nbsp; we/you/they <b>were/weren't</b>I <b>was</b> annoyed because they <b>were</b> late.<br><b>Was</b> the weather good when you <b>were</b> on holiday?<br>They <b>weren't</b> able to come because they <b>were</b> so busy.</div>
</section>

<section class="slide w">
<h2>Past Continuous (I was doing)</h2>
<p>Yesterday Karen and Joe played tennis. They started at 10 o'clock and finished at 11.30. So, at 10.30 they <b>were playing</b> tennis.</p>
<p>they were playing = they were in the middle of playing, they had not finished</p>
<table>
<tr><td>he/she/it</td><td><b>was</b></td><td>playing, doing, working etc.</td></tr>
<tr><td>we/you/they</td><td><b>were</b></td><td>playing, doing, working etc.</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="q" style="margin-top:12px">This time last year I <b>was living</b> in Hong Kong.<br>What <b>were</b> you <b>doing</b> at 10 o'clock last night?<br>I waved to Helen, but she <b>wasn't looking</b>.</div>
</section>

