<section class="slide b">
<h2>Some Verbs Are Not Used in Continuous Forms</h2>
<p>Some verbs (for example, <b>know</b> and <b>want</b>) are not normally used in continuous forms (is + -ing, was + -ing etc.).</p>
<div class="q">We were good friends. We <b>knew</b> each other well. <i class="rv">(not we were knowing)</i></div>
<div class="q">I was enjoying the party, but Chris <b>wanted</b> to go home. <i class="rv">(not was wanting)</i></div>
</section>

