<h2>Completion</h2>
<i class="s">Complete the story with the words provided. Put the words into the correct forms of simple past tense or past continuous tense. The following text is for questions number 13-18.</i>
<h3>The Origin of Kasada Ceremony in Tengger</h3>
<p>Long ago, in a village near Mount Bromo, there was a couple who had just recently married. Their names were Roro Anteng and Joko Seger. According to the story, Roro Anteng's father was a god who lived in the Penanjakan Mountains. Her mother was a beautiful village girl who lived alone in the Penanjakan Mountains.</p>
<p>Roro Anteng was beautiful. When she was born, she was a quiet baby, so her mother gave her the name Roro Anteng (a quiet one). Also according to legend, Joko Seger was a son of an ascetic. One day, the ascetic's wife gave birth to a boy. He was handsome, with a bright face. In fact, it was said that he was the son of a holy spirit. When he was born, he could already scream. He had a strong grasp and a strong kick. He was different from other children. Because of this, his parents decided to call him Joko Seger (a strong one).</p>
</section>

<section class="slide b">
<h3>The Origin of Kasada Ceremony in Tengger</h3>
<p>Time flew quickly. Joko Seger and Roro Anteng grew into adults. There was a lot of fuss when Roro Anteng (13) <span class="a rv">reached</span> (reach) a marriageable age as many young men (14) <span class="a rv">wanted</span> (want) to marry her.</p>
<p>Roro Anteng had already decided she was going to marry Joko Seger. After their wedding, Joko Seger and Roro Anteng lived in domestic harmony. They lived on the slopes of Mount Bromo, working on their land together to meet their needs. They helped their neighbors and set a good example for the community.</p>
<p>The villagers consulted them about all kinds of problems, from cultivation to animal husbandry. Joko Seger and Roro Anteng were happy with their activities. They lived contentedly, thanking the Great Creator for their blessed and comfortable life.</p>
<p>Years went by, and they grew old. Already the villagers had begun to call them Nyai and Kyai (meaning the elders). Still, they did not have any children. When they (15) <span class="a rv">went</span> (go) down to the village, the other families (16) <span class="a rv">were playing</span> (play) with their children. This would make them sad.</p>
</section>

<section class="slide w">
<h3>The Origin of Kasada Ceremony in Tengger</h3>
<p>"Look at that family, Nyai. They are happy with their son!"</p>
<p>"That's right, Kyai. Why hasn't God given us any children?" Then they agreed that they would ask God.</p>
<p>Nyai Anteng and Kyai Seger went to the foot of Mount Bromo and meditated. Every day, they prayed and meditated ceaselessly. Finally, the God Brahma answered their prayer. Nyai Anteng heard a voice telling her that she would have many children, but that she must sacrifice the youngest. She agreed. After that, Nyai Anteng began to have children.</p>
<p>Less than a year after her first baby, she had a second. Until finally, Nyai Anteng and Kyai Seger had twenty five children. Nyai Anteng and Kyai cared for their children and taught them lovingly. Their life was full of joy and happiness. Later on, their family formed the basis of the community of Tengger (from Anteng and Seger).</p>
<p>Everyone in the community descended from Nyai Anteng and Kyai Seger. When Kusuma, their youngest son, was born, they began to worry. They remembered their promise to Brahma. Kusuma was a good boy; strong and handsome. Every time they looked at him, they were sad.</p>
</section>

<section class="slide b">
<h3>The Origin of Kasada Ceremony in Tengger</h3>
<p>Then, one day, Nyai Anteng had the idea of moving to Mount Penanjakan to escape from Brahma. Kyai Seger agreed. They (17) <span class="a rv">were preparing</span> (prepare) for the move, taking what they would need, when they (18) <span class="a rv">heard</span> (hear) loud noises from deep in the heart of Mount Bromo before they were ready to leave for Penanjakan. Brahma was reminding them of their promise. Smoke billowed from the top of the mountain. Nyai and Kyai were scared.</p>
